title ALES48 — Lotus's parametric bell: the fixed-EQ family made whole
prompt keep taking the next Lindy-first crux-first Lotus lap, self-approve the design round, send each finished increment, stop only at the custody gates in REMEMBER
think After the band-pass (ALES46, keep the middle) and band-reject (ALES47, drop the middle), the Lindy-first culmination is the gesture that TURNS the middle — the parametric bell (peaking EQ), the most-reached-for tool in any mix.
think Design: keep the low and high edges at unity, scale the mid band by a gain. The mid is the exact residual M = x − L − H (ALES42 the stack's own lesson applied to two cutoffs instead of one split), so gaining only the middle can never disturb the edges and unity gain reconstructs by construction.
think Crux chosen: the bell IS the whole fixed-EQ family at three gains — unity gain = identity byte-for-byte; zero gain = ALES47's band-reject, proven by equality against notch.notch over a copy (the bell is the notch at zero gain); larger gain boosts the middle. This composition proof ties the three rungs together with no new arithmetic on the audio path.
obs A constant settles to itself at ANY gain because the middle is zero at direct current (M = x − x − 0 = 0) — proven at both a ×8 boost and a full cut, so the bell never moves the settled edges. Saturation proven with a wide alternating middle boosted ×20 pinning to the rail rather than wrapping.
obs Reused tone.precheck (ALES46) for both cutoffs, BellError = tone.ToneError || error{ BadGain } (the same fault the shelf/stack name), and notch.notch as the zero-gain equality target — so the witness proves the identity honest by re-running ALES47 green.
obs GREEN on the first build across six clauses; ALES47 band-reject re-run stays GREEN. TAME bans clean, zero-assert ratchet unchanged. Third rung of this turn (ALES46·47·48), each sent as its own signed round.
loom witness=ales_bell_witness green=1 clauses=6 rungs_reused=4 family=lowpass,highpass,shelf,stack,bandpass,bandreject,bell
file lotus/bell.rye the parametric bell — edges at unity, residual mid scaled by gain, unity=identity, zero=notch
file tools/ales_bell_witness.rish builds, runs the selftest, asserts GREEN ales-bell, re-proves ALES47 band-reject green
file active-designing/20260814-170143_fill-ales48-lotus-parametric-bell.md the self-approved design round for ALES48
file lotus/README.md front door synced — the ALES48 bell sentence, the fixed-EQ family named whole
recommend check-in the fixed-EQ family is whole (low-pass through parametric bell); the next natural cruxes — a moving centre (sweep the bell), a real hertz/Q, or gain automation under an envelope — all lean toward a real time base, a good place for Keaton to point the next journey
